{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792329582,"nonce":"Pb//iYlDUR0baNhCVjPedpYJ4GI=","title":"Tier-1 promotions run first come, first served: a large region compile delays the small hot functions behind it","message":"Promotions to the optimizing tier go through beadie's PromotionBroker, a bounded FIFO channel with one worker per broker, and through zyntax's own promotion and resume-point threads. A job's order is its arrival order, whatever it costs or saves.\n\nIn a 5-iteration run (CI's --fast) that decides which functions get LLVM code at all. raytrace-simple after 571cd3ff: the render frame leaves into its outlined region after 2 visits rather than 16, so Scene$render$trusted and Scene$render$trusted$resume1 are promoted early, and firstIntersection, SimpleSurface$colourAt, Vector$__add__, Ray$pointAtTime and others that main promotes within the run no longer are. NUC, 4 pinned cores, CI's figure: 1.097 against 7ac7d368, with the first iteration unchanged. meteor showed the same effect before the asking rule was narrowed: solve's promotion was submitted in both builds and reached LLVM in neither within 5 iterations, behind 30 to 75 ms compiles of get_footprints regions, setup code that had already finished.\n\nOptions: order the queue by expected benefit per compile cost (calls or back-edge visits since the request against instruction count); drop a job whose bead has had no calls or frames since it was queued, as the baseline queue already does (\"dropped compile of bead N: no calls since\"); do not compile a function and its outlined region at the tier both when only one is running.","files":null}]}